  "note": "Municipal election, January 1929. Not a single nomination was received for the six vacancies, so the retiring members were declared elected without a contest (Belfast News-Letter, 4 January 1929, p. 13). The returning officer, Mr. David Law, attended the Town Hall but received no nominations. The six retiring members were declared elected in due course. Returned unopposed."
